    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="callout info" style="margin-top:20px;">
    <strong>Key Insight:</strong> Air Jordan 11 Retro leads all models with a <strong>$99.84</strong> average profit and the highest premium rate (63.4%). Air Jordan 1 Low trails significantly at <strong>$50.52</strong>, despite having the second-highest transaction volume. The retail price floor is the differentiator: AJ1 Low's $125 MSRP sets a lower ceiling, while AJ11 Retro's $227 MSRP anchors higher absolute margins.
  </div>

